{"base_rate":0.16442048517520216,"brier":0.07085215633423181,"bss":0.4842854759386569,"bss_hi":0.5587997735925027,"bss_lo":0.38981546242311954,"chart":{"base":[275.2,50.3],"fp":[220.8,343.3],"lead":"62,251.4 272,236.6 482,204.7 692,138.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.48 — higher than 90% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end +6pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 49% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 2%; promised 66% → rained 63%"},"rel":"62,459.1 123.2,417.4 478.8,192.9"},"country":"ES","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.021388140161725057,"ess":371.47182258962005,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Murcia</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Murcia rain forecast is genuinely useful, and honest except at one point on the scale.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (86%), believe about\n<b>82%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 742 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMURCIA, 3.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.48, ranked 22 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(9&ndash;61) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>436</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>82%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Murcia</b> <span class=\"muted\">Spain</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">honest except at one point</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.48</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>9&ndash;61\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>742 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Murcia &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Murcia\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 70.6024,352.88 113.84815789473684,295.7894736842105 221.43,176.66666666666666 363.91116883116877,41.636363636363626 363.91116883116877,93.63636363636363 221.43,256.0 113.84815789473684,353.2631578947368 70.6024,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"322.1509433962264\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"322.1509433962264\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,376.1559633027523 70.6024,352.88 113.84815789473684,329.3157894736842 221.43,218.66666666666666 363.91116883116877,84.18181818181819\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 436 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"376.1559633027523\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"70.6024\" cy=\"352.88\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"113.84815789473684\" cy=\"329.3157894736842\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 46%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"221.43\" cy=\"218.66666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 86%&amp;#10;It rained 82% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"363.91116883116877\" cy=\"84.18181818181819\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(16%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Murcia the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.58) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.33).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.334</td><td class='num'>4.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'>0.429</td><td class='num'>4.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'>0.434</td><td class='num'>3.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>212</td><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'>0.580</td><td class='num'>1.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":37.98704,"lon":-1.13004,"n":742,"n_cities":213,"name":"Murcia","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":436,"obs":0.016055045871559634,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03559999999999999,"n":75,"obs":0.08,"sig":false},{"hi":0.3,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.15776315789473686,"n":76,"obs":0.14473684210526316,"sig":false},{"hi":0.68,"lo":0.3,"mean":0.4616666666666667,"n":78,"obs":0.44871794871794873,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.68,"mean":0.864155844155844,"n":77,"obs":0.8181818181818182,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":3.9,"provisional":false,"rank":22,"rank_hi":61.0,"rank_lo":9.0,"reliability":0.0006050668878824155,"resolution":0.06654417000467239,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"murcia","station":"MURCIA","timezone":"Europe/Madrid"}